{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>A soul, when it sins, and hears the voice of an oath.</b> They said in the Midrash: Come and see that when the supernal beings and the lower beings were created, they were created with half of the Name, as it says (Isaiah 26:4): ״כי ביה ה' צור עולמים״ — do not read צור (Rock) but צר (Creator); and why were they not created with the whole Name in its entirety? So as not to mention in it the complete Name. Woe to the wicked, who blaspheme the Name of the Holy One, blessed be He, and mention it constantly in vain! See what is written concerning the offerings of a man: ״כי יקריב מכם קרבן לה׳״ — it does not say לה׳ קרבן, לה׳ עולה, yet the children of men blaspheme His Name in vain. This is what Solomon, peace be upon him, said (Ecclesiastes 5:1): ״אל תבהל על פיך ולבך אל ימהר להוציא דבר לפני האלהים.״ Our Rabbis, of blessed memory, taught: A person in Israel should not be loose with vows, nor should he persist in oaths even concerning the truth. And there is an incident involving the King's Mountain, where there were two thousand towns, and all of them were destroyed because of the oath of truth. How so? A person would say to his fellow: I swear I am going to such-and-such a place, and I will eat and drink — and they would go and do so and fulfill their oath. And if one who swears in truth is treated thus, how much more so one who swears falsely! When the Holy One, blessed be He, comes to judge the creatures, He judges those who swear falsely together with the sorcerers and the adulterers, as it is written (Malachi 3:5): ״וקרבתי אליכם למשפט והייתי עד ממהר במכשפים ובמנאפים ובנשבעים לשקר.״ Said the Holy One, blessed be He: The mouth that I gave you to praise and extol Me with it — with it you blaspheme and revile and swear falsely in My Name! For all the creatures I created to praise Me, as it says (Proverbs 16:4): ״כל פעל ה' למענהו״ — and it is not enough for you that you do not praise Me, but you even blaspheme Me! And this is what is written (Isaiah 57:20): ״והרשעים כים נגרש כי השקט לא יוכל ויגרשו מימיו רפש וטיט״. Just as with this sea, the waves within it swell and rise, and when each one of them reaches the shore it breaks, and its fellow sees it broken and itself swells and rises and does not turn back — so the wicked see one another swelling and do not turn back; therefore they are likened to the sea, and they have no rest in the world, ״כי השקט לא יוכל״. But the righteous have rest, as it says (Jeremiah 30:10): ״ושב יעקב ושקט ושאנן ואין מחריד.״" "<b>And he is a witness, or saw, or knew.</b> The Ramban, of blessed memory, explained that these are not three separate matters, for there is no witness without sight and without knowledge; rather it says: if he heard the voice of an oath that was sworn upon him to adjure him concerning a matter in which he is a witness, whether by knowledge or by sight — if he does not tell, he bears his iniquity." "<b>And the truth is</b> that concerning the principal of money, it is impossible for there to be a witness without sight and without knowledge. But it is possible to understand from the language of Scripture three separate matters, each independent of the other: testimony on its own, sight without knowledge, and knowledge without sight, and testimony without sight and without knowledge. Sight without knowledge: for example, he saw him give a maneh in his presence, but he did not know whether it was a loan or a repayment or a deposit, he being an agent on behalf of another to receive from him. Knowledge without sight: for example, so-and-so admitted in his presence that he borrowed a maneh, but he did not see the money. Testimony without sight and without knowledge: this is the signature of witnesses, which this person recognizes — and his testimony benefits the litigant even though it involves neither sight nor knowledge, and on the basis of his testimony they remove the money from the other's possession. And this is: ״והוא עד או ראה או ידע.״ And our Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded: ״אם לוא יגיד״ — in the place fit to tell, that is, in a court of law; so if he suppressed his testimony between himself and the other, he is not punished for it, but only when he suppresses his testimony in a court of law, analogous to the case of Achan with Joshua, who was not liable for that telling except in Joshua's court. And this is what is written (Joshua 7:19): ״והגד נא לי מה עשית״ — two litigants and one witness and three judges of the court make six; therefore the vav was added to it: והגד נא לי, and it does not say הגד נא לי. And so here too it is written ״אם לוא יגיד״ — with a vav, meaning: if he does not tell in the court of law, ״ונשא עונו״ — this teaches you that the telling must be in a court of law, for together with them they are six." "<b>And it is also possible</b> to explain further: ״והוא עד״ — for the meaning of the verse is that if he suppresses his testimony and does not tell it in court, one should not say, 'And who knows about this matter whether he is suppressing testimony?' Therefore it says ״והוא עד״ — 'He' is the Name of the Holy One, blessed be He, a witness. For thus we find the expression הוא to be His Name, of the Holy One, blessed be He, from what is written (Isaiah 42:8): ״אני ה' הוא שמי״; and it is written (Psalms 100): ״הוא עשנו ולו אנחנו״; and it is written (Psalms 19): ״והוא כחתן יוצא מחופתו״; and it is written (Numbers 18:23): ״ועבד הלוי הוא״; and many more like these. Therefore it says ״והוא עד״ — His Name, of the Holy One, blessed be He, is עד (witness), for He examines hearts and kidneys, and will punish him for this." "<b>And it is also possible</b> to say further that the addition of the vav in the word לוא alludes to the six days of Genesis, and it comes to teach that one who suppresses testimony for his fellow — Scripture reckons it against him as though he suppressed testimony from the Holy One, blessed be He, concerning the renewal of the world that was created in six days. For through habituation to stumbling in a light transgression, a person comes in the end to stumble in a grave one."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:23:14.343405065Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}